# SelectIQ — Cursor Rules
# Auto-read by Cursor on every interaction.
# Backup implementation config. Primary tool is Claude Code (reads CLAUDE.md).

## Project
SelectIQ — AI-powered Campus Recruitment & Assessment Platform for Indian engineering colleges.

## Stack (Non-Negotiable — Never Suggest Alternatives)
- Framework: Next.js (App Router only — no `pages/` directory)
- Auth: Firebase Auth (Google OAuth + GitHub OAuth + Phone OTP via MSG91 custom tokens)
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL
- File Storage: Supabase Storage
- ORM: Prisma (ALL database access — no exceptions)
- Hosting: Vercel
- Code Execution: Judge0 CE (self-hosted)
- Secure Exam Browser: Electron (already built — do not rebuild)
- Excluded: Neon, Cloudflare R2, Supabase Auth, Drizzle, Knex, raw SQL

## Data Access Rules
- Prisma → ALL database reads/writes/migrations
- Supabase client → ONLY file storage (upload, download, signed URLs)
- Firebase Admin SDK → ONLY auth (verify tokens, create custom tokens)
- NEVER use Supabase client for database queries
- NEVER use Firebase for data storage

## Coding Rules
- TypeScript everywhere — no plain JavaScript
- Use App Router (`src/app/`) — never `pages/`
- Prisma client singleton at `src/lib/prisma.ts`
- Always verify Firebase ID token on server-side before processing requests
- Always use parameterized queries via Prisma
- Never hardcode secrets — use environment variables
- Never prefix server-only keys with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- Never commit `.env.local`
- Run `npx prisma generate` after any schema change
- Run `npx prisma migrate dev` after any schema change in development

## File Restrictions
- NEVER modify: `.cursorrules`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/project-context.md` without explicit instruction
- Always confirm build passes before reporting completion
- Report exact files created/modified/deleted after every task

## Workflow
- Plans come from Claude (claude.ai) — follow them exactly
- If plan is ambiguous, ask — do not guess
- Do not install packages not specified in the plan without asking
- After task completion, provide list of files changed for documentation
